The `description` given for that Bash call (seq 264) was:

**"Extract per-turn input distributions"**

For context, that's the command that ran:

```js
node -e "
const fs = require('fs');
const all = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('.../scratchpad/all-runs.json','utf8'));
const inputs = (label, arm) => all.perRun.filter(r => r.label===label && r.arm===arm).flatMap(r => r.turns.map(t => t.usage.input));
console.log('CT5='+JSON.stringify(inputs('iter5','context-tree')));
console.log('CT6='+JSON.stringify(inputs('iter6','context-tree')));
"
```

It loaded the previously exported `all-runs.json` (from `ct-stats.mjs --json`), filtered the per-run records to the context-tree arms of iter5 and iter6, flattened their per-turn `usage.input` values, and printed them as `CT5=` and `CT6=` arrays. Those arrays became the `CT5IN`/`CT6IN` constants in the report's fresh-input histogram (v3.1 marching to ~15k/turn vs v5 staying under ~4k).
